WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.720
“Ready up, squadron,” came the command
through the team’s headsets.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.910
“Check your gear and prep for departure.”

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.240
Meyers started methodically securing the various
pouches of her assault vest, tightening the

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.849
straps of her tactical garb and making sure
she could quickly reach her spare ammo, just

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:17.240
in case the mission went sideways.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.710
Beside her, the rest of the Deltas on the
team were doing the same, buckling into their

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.529
seats or checking their weapons were locked
and loaded.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:29.690
Sat on the opposite side of the aircraft,
Cole had his helmet and mask off, loudly chewing

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.829
on gum with his mouth open, showing off the
disgusting contents.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:37.829
When her eyes drifted over him, he tried to
give her a wink, resulting in Meyers rolling

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:38.829
her eyes.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:42.980
“You know, you should really close your
mouth when you do that, Cole,” she said,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.940
to which he sheered back at her.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.350
“Your face looks like a clogged garbage
disposal.”

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.870
“Cut the chatter!”

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.620
Gamma Leader interrupted; they weren’t present
with the team, instead coordinating their

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.060
movements from the safety of an undisclosed
location through their headsets.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.649
“Do I need to remind you that this isn’t
a field trip, Delta Unit?”

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:03.750
“Sir, no sir,” Meyers replied, gritting
her teeth.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.960
“Good, now then, all of you listen up and
listen good,” the voice continued.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.940
“This operation has been approved by The
Engineer himself, so let’s keep it quick,

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.159
clean, and quiet.

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:16.800
You all know your target: SCP-096.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:23.009
You are to enter Site 19, capture the creature
and deliver it to our client, Valentin Zukovich,

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:24.400
at the rendezvous location.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.590
The use of deadly force against Foundation
personnel is, as always, authorized.”

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.420
The team already knew all of this.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.150
They’d been over it in their briefing before.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:40.210
But the Insurgency demanded total efficiency
and zero ambiguity about the Delta’s objective.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:44.710
“Now, each of you has been issued with a
pair of live feed goggles,” Gamma Leader

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.590
explained; as they described them, Meyers
and the other members of the team all produced

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.590
their goggles.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.640
“As you know, these aren’t just relaying
your visuals to us here.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.159
Your goggles have a camera lens at the front,
and will transmit that feed directly to your

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:58.159
eyes.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:01.439
Given the nature of the SCP we’re going
after, the goggles have been programmed to

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:07.130
detect faces and pixelate them, so that should
circumvent any problems created by the creature’s

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.619
anomalous abilities.”

00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:12.360
Meyers slipped her goggles over her eyes and
flipped the switch to activate them.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.400
Immediately, her vision was filled with a
feed of Cole directly opposite her.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.980
Only now, his entire face had been obscured,
replaced with a digital jumble of pixels.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.430
It was exactly like the cop shows she used
to watch as a kid, how they would blur out

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.170
a suspect’s face to hide their identity.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.910
Delta Meyers smirked, glad that she could
no longer see Cole’s face.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:36.069
“Well, this is a definite improvement, Cole,”
she taunted.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:39.200
“Now, I don’t have to look at you chewing
with your mouth open.”

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.470
“Another important reminder,” Gamma Leader
announced.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.530
“Mister Zukovich is one of the Chaos Insurgency’s
wealthiest benefactors.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.090
He’s not just offered us funding in exchange
for undertaking this mission, but if you pull

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.500
this off, he’ll grant us access to his fellow
oligarchs.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.409
That means more people to offer potential
investment in the Insurgency.

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:01.970
So, remember, Delta Unit: we have a lot riding
on this.”

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:07.060
With that, the aircraft began to whirr into
life, lifting upwards off the ground.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.870
The Insurgency had been developing this new
high-speed stealth craft for a while, a modified

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.870
troop carrier that was capable of both vertical
take-off and landing.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:20.410
The technicians had boasted it could reach
supersonic flight speeds in seconds, effectively

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:24.860
launching Chaos Insurgents at enemy locations,
where they could be deployed, complete their

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.870
objective and escape in the craft all within
a matter of minutes.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:33.410
“Oh, and one more thing,” Gamma Leader
stated as the stealth craft climbed higher.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:37.810
“We have a contact within Site 19; Junior
Researcher Bartrum.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.799
He’s agreed to let you in.

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:43.920
Of course, the last thing we want is the Foundation
squeezing any info out of him after you’ve

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:44.920
departed.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.920
You know what to do.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.120
Safe travels, Delta Unit.”

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:52.170
A building mechanical sound of rapid acceleration
filled the stealth craft, followed by a loud

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.709
boom as the engines kicked into gear.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:59.640
Inside, Meyers and her fellow members of the
Chaos Insurgency – Deltas Griffith, Slater,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.280
and Cole – all gripped their seats tightly
as they were rocked by the extreme force of

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.700
the craft’s speed.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.120
It shot through the sky, hurtling towards
the coordinates of its target, reaching Mach

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.840
3 in a manner of seconds.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.190
Outside the hull, a sonic boom rang out like
the foreboding sound of an ominous thundercrack.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:23.440
Invisible to radar, sonar, and even protected
against most anomalous forms of detection,

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.570
the stealth craft zipped through the air,
gradually lowering its breakneck speed as

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.860
it came within several miles of Site 19.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:35.600
Continuing its approach, the aircraft slowed
to a hovering stop above the Foundation facility.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.820
Unbuckling from their seats, each of the Deltas
made their way to the ramp opening up at the

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:45.620
rear of the craft, and began to descend a
cable, lower and lower towards the roof.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.780
Junior Researcher Bartrum had been pacing
nervously back and forth near the door that

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.660
led from the roof to a stairwell down into
Site 19.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.660
He’d had to tell his fellow Foundation staff
that he needed a cigarette break, despite

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.660
not actually being a smoker.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.990
As he waited for the Insurgency’s arrival,
he couldn’t stop himself from trembling,

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.600
only to turn and feel his heart jump in his
chest at the sight of the Delta Unit approaching

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.600
him.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.600
“You Bartrum?”

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.760
Griffith asked.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.800
“Y-yeah,” the researcher nodded awkwardly.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.699
“We need your key-card,” the Delta stated.

00:05:09.699 --> 00:05:10.699
“Oh, yeah.

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:11.699
Sure thing.”

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:15.259
Bartrum rummaged through his pockets, producing
his Foundation issue ID and handing it over.

00:05:15.259 --> 00:05:18.330
It wasn’t until the card left his fingers
that a thought struck him.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.660
“Wait, the security system logs where personnel
tap in their card.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.110
If you use mine to spring 096, they’ll think
it was me who did it.”

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:29.630
“That’s the idea,” Slater replied apathetically
as Griffith raised his weapon and fired a

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.110
single, silenced shot.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.220
After dragging Bartrum’s body away, the
team used his card to unlock the roof door

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.490
and make their way down the stairwell.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.949
Each one of them knew the way, they had all
been to Site 19 plenty of times before back

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:42.949
in the day.

00:05:42.949 --> 00:05:47.190
You see, of all things with an equal and opposite
reaction in the universe, the Foundation’s

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.970
was born out of their own organization.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:55.190
The Chaos Insurgency had begun its life as
part of the SCP Foundation, an off-the-books

00:05:55.190 --> 00:06:00.440
black ops unit created by the mysterious,
illusive O5 Council as a front to carry out

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.720
some of the organization's more nefarious
activities.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:09.979
But the original Insurgency ultimately defected,
breaking away from the Foundation and becoming

00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:11.479
a splinter group.

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:16.740
Their sole purpose was to eliminate their
rivals, the SCP Foundation, and they’d utilize

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.570
any means – even their own anomalies – to
achieve that goal.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:26.550
Like many others within the Insurgency’s
ranks, Meyers, Griffith, Slater and Cole had

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.819
been scouted while they were still a part
of the Foundation.

00:06:29.819 --> 00:06:33.830
Each of the Delta Unit had either formerly
been security personnel or a Mobile Task Force

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:39.180
operator, meaning they had skills that made
them useful to the Chaos Insurgency.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:43.030
On top of that, they’d all become disillusioned
with Foundation.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:46.190
Its constant secrecy and lies were frustrating
enough.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:50.539
But their dangerous anomalous experiments,
all the deaths they had caused, directly or

00:06:50.539 --> 00:06:54.540
indirectly, had highlighted something far
worse to the Deltas.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:59.919
The Foundation placed more importance on the
containment in ‘SCP’ than protecting the

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:00.919
world.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:04.530
Moving silently through the halls of Site
19, keeping their formation tight to cover

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:07.020
all angles in front and behind them.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.889
Slater gave a hand signal, indicating they
were free to go ‘weapons hot’ if they

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:15.629
encountered any Foundation personnel on their
way towards their target.

00:07:15.629 --> 00:07:20.569
Meyers still had her goggles active, even
though they hadn’t reached SCP-096’s cell

00:07:20.569 --> 00:07:21.569
yet.

00:07:21.569 --> 00:07:25.110
Even though she despised the Foundation and
what they had done, not being able to see

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.699
the faces of passing researchers and security
personnel made it a little easier to pull

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:30.699
the trigger.

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:33.770
The team approached the airtight steel cube
that housed their target.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.970
All of the Deltas knew they needed to be quick;
while there were no recording or surveillance

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:42.500
devices inside the creature’s cell, it wouldn’t
take long for the Foundation to spot the trail

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.419
of bodies the team had left on their way down.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:50.349
Griffith gave a nod for the others to activate
their goggles, his face already a scrambled,

00:07:50.349 --> 00:07:52.560
pixelated blur from Meyers’s point of view.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.830
Then, with a wave of the stolen key card,
the door to the cell opened.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.699
As you may have already gathered, the goggles
being worn by the Deltas were actually based

00:08:00.699 --> 00:08:05.830
on a pre-existing Foundation technology - The
infamous SCRAMBLE goggles brought to us by

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.110
the highly duplicitous Dr. Dan.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:13.930
However, as anyone familiar with 096’s files
know, those goggles were imperfect creations,

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.940
and got a lot of MTF Operatives killed.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:21.420
However, scientists paid off by the deep pockets
of Chaos Insurgency benefactors had worked

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:27.740
tirelessly on improving the technology, until
they finally made for a viable 096 protective

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.740
device.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:34.180
Still, even with the goggles masking its haunting,
wide-jawed face, and even after Cole had gently

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.899
thrown a hood over the Shy Guy’s face, Meyers
couldn’t bring herself to look at it for

00:08:38.899 --> 00:08:39.899
too long.

00:08:39.899 --> 00:08:44.921
It felt wrong, like it was forbidden, despite
knowing it wouldn’t harm her or the other

00:08:44.921 --> 00:08:48.550
Delta’s unless they looked directly at its
face.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:53.950
SCP-096 was usually docile and calm when unobserved,
and while it didn’t seem to be anywhere

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.810
near as agitated as it got whenever its face
was seen, the towering creature was notably

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:03.760
confused as Slater looped a leash around its
neck and started guiding it out of the cell

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.920
with an animal control pole.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:10.240
Suddenly, the alarms started blaring: the
Foundation knew they were there.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.190
The Shy Guy still didn’t become enraged,
but began sobbing slightly underneath the

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:15.600
hood covering it.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.890
“Move, move!”

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:21.019
Meyers shouted over the noise, as the Delta’s
started doubling back the way they had come.

00:09:21.019 --> 00:09:25.140
Traversing the corridors back towards the
stairwell, any of the pixel-faced Foundation

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:29.180
staff that the Insurgents saw was quickly
dispatched, bullets being spat out of the

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.850
barrels of their weapons.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:35.060
As the Delta’s reached the roof, the stealth
craft was waiting for them, as they quickly

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:38.130
boarded with SCP-096 in tow.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:43.040
It sat at the far end of the craft, hunched
over itself, rocking back and forth slightly

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.450
as the troop carrier took off and shot towards
its next destination.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:50.970
“Nice work, Delta Unit,” Gamma Leader
congratulated the team over their headsets.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.440
“There’s been a slight change of plans.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.290
Mister Zukovich has requested us to forego
meeting at the agreed rendezvous.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:00.810
He wants you to bring SCP-096 to him directly.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.519
He’s arriving at his compound as we speak.”

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:07.230
That was the part of the whole operation that
didn’t sit right with Meyers at all.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:11.580
They had just risked their lives to secure
the Shy Guy, only to hand him over to some

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.060
wealthy oligarch.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:16.770
It didn’t seem to make sense, or align with
the Insurgency’s goals.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.290
“With respect, sir,” she spoke up.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.230
“What benefit is this to us?

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:22.760
Why turn over the anomaly to Zukovich?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.519
What does he want with it?”

00:10:24.519 --> 00:10:28.720
“What Mister Zukovich wants is none of our
concern, Delta Meyers,” the mission co-ordinator

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:29.760
retorted abruptly.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:34.191
“And as for the ‘why’, he’s worth
billions to us as a continued ally, so I’d

00:10:34.191 --> 00:10:36.980
advise you to watch your tone unless-”
“Money?”

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:37.980
Meyers interrupted.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.370
“Is that seriously the only reason we’re
doing this?

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.589
The Chaos Insurgency aren’t supposed to
be mercenaries!

00:10:42.589 --> 00:10:46.860
We’re meant to be harming the Foundation,
using anomalies as tools to achieve that goal.”

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:52.110
There was a few long, awkward seconds of radio
silence, the other Delta’s staring uncertainly

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.779
at Meyers, too cowardly to speak up.

00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:59.029
“You’re right,” Gamma Leader replied,
ending the uncomfortable pause; their tone

00:10:59.029 --> 00:11:04.020
was an unnerving calm, like they were holding
back from letting loose in rage.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:07.790
“Anomalies are useful tools for us achieving
what we need.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:12.880
And right now, what the Insurgency needs is
to secure funding from Valentin Zukovich and

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.639
his fellow wealthy compatriots.

00:11:14.639 --> 00:11:20.050
So, for the last time, deliver the package
as instructed.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.589
Or face a reprimand.”

00:11:22.589 --> 00:11:26.240
Arriving outside the compound, walls with
barbed wire at the top towering over their

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:32.650
stealth craft, the team marched towards the
front gate, guiding SCP-096 along by its neck.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:36.920
The creature seemed to have calmed down, barely
making much in the way of noise, even with

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.130
the hood muffling it.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:43.089
But that calm did little to settle the tension
Meyers still felt, and neither did the arrival

00:11:43.089 --> 00:11:47.510
of Zukovich’s aide, coming out to lead the
Deltas into one of the many buildings of the

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.779
wealthy oligarch’s complex.

00:11:49.779 --> 00:11:54.000
The doors to the building opened, and a cacophony
of noise came flooding out.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:58.450
Screeching, roaring, howling, so loud it was
almost deafening.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.940
Inside was like a zoo, or a zoo without enclosures.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:07.080
All around, exotic animals were held in cramped
cages, empty of anything save for the wildlife

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.089
they house.

00:12:08.089 --> 00:12:13.449
There were lions, tigers, bears – oh yes,
and many more besides.

00:12:13.449 --> 00:12:18.300
Each one of them was illegally imported or
stolen, all now contributing to the exotic

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.160
menagerie of one Valentin Zukovich.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.000
“Welcome, welcome, my friends!”

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:28.300
the billionaire greeted them eagerly, his
thick-accented voice booming, just audible

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.520
against the various animal noises.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.470
“The operatives of the Chaos Insurgency
for you, sir,” the aide announced as he

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.529
gestured his hands towards the Delta Unit.

00:12:36.529 --> 00:12:39.300
“Excellent, yes, yes, very good.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:44.270
Get these hard-working people the case, Anatoly,”
Zukovich replied with a swat of his hand.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:46.440
“Now, let me see what you have brought.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.089
Let me look at my newest pet!”

00:12:48.089 --> 00:12:50.660
“He wants it as a pet?”

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.610
Meyers heard Cole mutter next to her.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:57.750
Zukovich looked at SCP-096 with wonder; it
was clear he had never seen a creature like

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.360
it, but had no doubt heard the stories of
what it could do.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:05.019
Reaching out a hand, the wealthy oligarch
gently patted at the creature’s hairless

00:13:05.019 --> 00:13:06.019
skin.

00:13:06.019 --> 00:13:09.720
“So docile,” he remarked in surprise when
the Shy Guy did little to react.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.640
“Why is has bag over head?”

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:16.120
A collective split second’s panic hit every
one of the Deltas as they watched Zukovich’s

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.410
hand reaching up to lift the hood from SCP-096’s
face.

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:24.010
It was Slater who reacted first, grabbing
the billionaire by the wrist, stopping him

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:25.190
before it was too late.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:29.380
“Sorry, sir, but I don’t think that’s
an advisable idea,” he said, releasing the

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.380
man’s hand.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:33.459
Zukovich paused for a second, an angered look
on his face.

00:13:33.459 --> 00:13:39.010
Suddenly, he launched a fist at Slater, gripped
him by his uniform then struck again and again.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:43.440
As their benefactor kept punching him, Slater
screamed in pain until he couldn’t anymore,

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.880
a sickening gurgle taking its place.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.860
When he was finally released, he fell to the
floor, still.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:54.680
“Is not ‘advisable idea’ to touch me
either,” Zukovich scoffed, spitting on Slater’s

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.680
body.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.810
“We meant no disrespect, Mister Zukovich,”
Meyers spoke up.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.110
“It’s just, you shouldn’t provoke it.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:05.050
Anyone who looks at SCP-096 face… dies.”

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:09.570
The oligarch turned to face her; his anger
suddenly replaced worryingly fast with a look

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.570
of curiosity.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:11.570
“Really?

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:12.899
Tell me, how they die?

00:14:12.899 --> 00:14:17.280
Instant, like heart attack?” he asked, mimicking
a death rattle then chuckling.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:21.000
“No, sir, it… finds them,” she replied.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.320
“Reports differ, some indicate it kills
anyone that sees its face with its bare hands.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.519
The exact method is unclear, because there
are never bodies.

00:14:28.519 --> 00:14:30.620
It never leaves any trace.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.080
If you see its face, it’ll annihilate you
completely.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.399
That’s why they call it the Shy Guy.”

00:14:35.399 --> 00:14:37.040
“Heh, ‘Shy Guy’.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.370
I like this,” Zukovich laughed.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.850
“It harder to kill from inside a cage.”

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.450
“I don’t think it matters.”

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:47.300
Meyer thought about shooting back with that,
but instead kept it in.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:50.579
At that moment, Zukovich’s aide returned,
carrying a steel carry case.

00:14:50.579 --> 00:14:55.040
He reached around it and unclipped the lid,
showing off rows of hundred dollar bills,

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.509
bound together in stacks.

00:14:56.509 --> 00:14:59.430
“Fair day’s pay for fair day’s work,
yes?”

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:00.610
Zukovich announced.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:03.399
As Cole went to collect the case, the aide
snapped it shut again.

00:15:03.399 --> 00:15:07.980
“There is just one more favor I ask you
to do for me,” the oligarch announced.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.279
“I host party tonight, big party!

00:15:10.279 --> 00:15:12.050
I want to show off my new…

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.050
what you called it?

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.050
Shy Guy!

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:17.610
My friends are all very wealthy, could offer
money to your Insurgency.”

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:22.079
“With all due respect,” Meyers found herself
echoing the phrase for a second time that

00:15:22.079 --> 00:15:26.060
day; without holding any respect for either
of the people it had been directed at.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.980
“The Chaos Insurgency is not your private
security force.”

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.630
“Delta Meyers, quiet!”

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.680
Gamma Leader hissed in her earpiece.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:36.440
“Zukovich’s connections could lead to
potentially billions – no, trillions – worth

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.839
of financial backing for the Insurgency.

00:15:38.839 --> 00:15:43.779
You will do as he asks, or so help me, I’ll
kill you myself.”

00:15:43.779 --> 00:15:48.640
A few hours after begrudgingly agreeing, Meyer
found herself standing in the menagerie room,

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:53.360
itching in the suit Zukovich’s staff had
instructed her and the other Deltas to wear.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:57.850
All around her were more wealthy, corrupt
figures with close ties – and similarly

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.500
sized bank accounts – to Zukovich.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:05.579
The guests were milling about, drinking flutes
of expensive champagne, observing the captive

00:16:05.579 --> 00:16:09.000
animals up-close, or taunting them in their
cages.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:12.810
In the center of the room, a new cage had
been placed with a shroud covering it and

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:13.810
SCP-096 inside.

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:14.810
“Friends!”

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:15.810
Zukovich announced, swaying slightly, evidently
drunk – as if the champagne bottle in his

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:16.810
hand wasn’t enough of a sign.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:19.450
“Today is a great day!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:25.259
Thanks to my friends in the Chaos Insurgency,
I am now the proud owner of a creature like

00:16:25.259 --> 00:16:26.300
no other.”

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:31.000
He staggered towards the covered cage, gripping
the shroud covering it in his free hand, taking

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.000
another swig before he continued.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.240
“I present to you: the Shy Guy!”

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:38.350
He pulled the cover away, met with a few scattered
sounds of confusion and surprise from his

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.759
rich guests.

00:16:39.759 --> 00:16:43.720
Only one or two made frightened gasps at the
sight of what was within.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:48.980
Sure enough, there, sitting timidly in its
cage, was SCP-096.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:52.070
It was calm, its face still covered with the
hood.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:55.110
“It’s just sitting there,” one of the
guests yelled.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.579
“Hardly very impressive.”

00:16:56.579 --> 00:16:59.029
“What does it do, Valentin?”

00:16:59.029 --> 00:17:01.370
another of his wealthy compatriots asked.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:06.140
“Well, it… ah, it mostly just sort of…
sits there,” Zukovich replied in his inebriated

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:08.990
state, before turning to look at the tall,
humanoid creature.

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:13.449
Suddenly, without warning and by force of
some intoxicated thought, he hurled his champagne

00:17:13.449 --> 00:17:14.449
bottle at the creature.

00:17:14.449 --> 00:17:15.449
“Do something!

00:17:15.449 --> 00:17:17.630
Entertain my guests!” he yelled, slurring
his words.

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:21.160
The glass bottle hit SCP-096 and shattered.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:26.150
Instantly, the creature recoiled, howling
in pain, met with more taunting laughter from

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.059
the gathered guests watching it.

00:17:28.059 --> 00:17:33.179
It started shaking and sobbing heavily, weeping
loudly, which only elicited more laughs from

00:17:33.179 --> 00:17:34.179
them all.

00:17:34.179 --> 00:17:39.410
But Meyers and the other Deltas weren’t
laughing, instead looking in horror as SCP-096

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:44.190
drew itself up to its full, towering height…
and pulled off its hood.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:49.179
It stared with sunken eyes at the crowd, their
taunts petering off and turning to silence

00:17:49.179 --> 00:17:50.880
for a moment.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.360
“Heh, not so shy now, yes?”

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.970
Zukovich laughed drunkenly.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.419
Then in screamed.

00:17:58.419 --> 00:18:03.880
SCP-096 went into a fit of rageful despair,
dashing through the bars of its cage and immediately

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.610
dispatching Zukovich.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:09.851
The wealthy guests all began screaming in
horror at what was happening, as the Shy Guy

00:18:09.851 --> 00:18:15.650
raced up to each of them one by one, killing
them all in a chain reaction for looking at

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:16.650
its face.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:20.220
Meyers dashed for the exit; aware she didn’t
have her goggles to block the sight of the

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:22.929
creature’s wide-jawed, screaming expression.

00:18:22.929 --> 00:18:27.159
Maybe if she could get far away, the stealth
craft could take her anywhere, maybe fast

00:18:27.159 --> 00:18:30.470
enough to evade the Insurgency and SCP-096.

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:34.350
She thought the Shy Guy was too busy with
the assembled guests of the now-deceased Zukovich

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.830
and that would mean she could slip away unscathed.

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:41.020
It was only when she saw in appear in front
of her in the blink of an eye, screeching

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:45.970
in despair as it towered over Meyers, that
she realized she had thought wrong…

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:53.230
Now go check out “SCP-096 A LESSON IN POWER”
and “SCP-096 PICTURE PERFECT” for more

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.000
stories of everyone’s favorite homicidal
introvert!

